If some enumerated neighbourhood is contained in the intersection of two enumerated
neighbourhoods, then the enumeration at their intersection index equals that
intersection.

The level set of the raw intersection code is nonempty, because that level set is the
intersection and consistency is equivalent to nonemptiness of the intersection.
Unfolding the intersection index and rewriting by invariance of the enumeration under
canonicalization reduces the claim to the level set of the canonicalized raw code.
Nonemptiness removes that canonicalization, and the raw code presents the intersection.
